## Errors & Mistakes
- Import-smoke first tried `import multistorageclient.torch` -> ModuleNotFoundError. The DCP module
  is NOT a direct submodule; it's a lazy attribute alias (msc.torch -> multistorageclient.contrib.torch
  via top-level __getattr__). storage.py uses attribute access (_msc().torch.X), which is correct.
- A research agent initially claimed MSC's torch extra is `torch<3,>=2.11`; adversarial verify REFUTED
  the version claim (repo main is now `>=2.12.1`). Resolution: pin `>=0.50.0,<1` (the 0.50.0 RELEASE's
  torch extra is torch<3,>=2.11, accepts target torch 2.11.0); re-check resolved version at install.

## Dead Ends
- Considered an "MSC-via-fsspec shim" (keep storage.py ~identical, route through MSC's fsspec
  protocol). Rejected: MSC's only supported DCP integration is the explicit writer/reader objects,
  not an msc:// checkpoint_id string, so a shim can't cover the load-bearing shard I/O.
- Considered "drop s3:// entirely, msc:// only". Rejected once research showed s3:// works through MSC
  implicit profiles with zero config file. Kept s3:// scheme; dropped only the fsspec/s3fs backend.

## Hints for Future Agents
- storage.dcp_save/dcp_load pass storage_writer/storage_reader ONLY for remote and checkpoint_id ONLY
  for local. Do not pass both (DCP ambiguity). The writer/reader carry the path.
- msc.list(base, include_directories=True) returns ObjectMetadata whose .key is canonicalized to
  msc://<profile>/... even for an s3:// base; that key feeds straight back into msc.delete.
- msc.delete raises FileNotFoundError on a missing path -> callers must catch broadly.
- The `msc` extra installs multi-storage-client (PyPI name has hyphens; import name is multistorageclient).

## Codebase Discoveries
- torch.distributed.checkpoint natively consumed fsspec s3:// as checkpoint_id (how the fsspec branch
  worked); MSC does NOT, hence the writer/reader indirection.
- botocore has no AWS_*ADDRESSING* env var; addressing_style config var maps env slot None
  (configprovider.py:212). Custom endpoint auto-forces path-style (utils.py:2633). AWS_CA_BUNDLE and
  AWS_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION ARE env-settable.

